<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104709" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρήρων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>timorous, shy,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always epith. of doves (i. e. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιστεραί,</span> the genus of which <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλειαι</span> are a species, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1262.61
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρήρωσι πελειάσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.778
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				114
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				575
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλειαι τρήρωνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.63
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρήρωνα πέλειαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.140
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				23.853
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.541
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέπφοι τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					1067
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> fem.
				Subst.
			<i>trembler,</i>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιστερά</span>
			 (metaph. of women), <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				87
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				423
			</span></i>. (Since the Subst. is implied for <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυτρήρων, τ.</span> is perh.
			always a Subst., name of the genus, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. πελειάδες</span> is to be compared with
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴρηξ κίρκος, σῦς κάπρος,</span>
			etc.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
